  "query_preview": "(Saturday through Tuesday)...\nFriday night will be slightly warmer with not much change in high\ntemperatures on Saturday. Moderate HeatRisk will continue on\nSaturday for the same areas as on Friday, coastal areas and \nportions of the western valleys in San Diego County and in \nportions of inland Orange County.\n\nMid and high clouds from tropical moisture and a low pressure \nsystem moving inland along the West Coast will spread cooling \ninland on Sunday and Monday. High temperatures on Sunday will cool\na few degrees near the coast to as much as 4 to 8 degrees for the\ninland valleys with high temperatures cooling a few more degrees \non Monday. With the cooling, high temperatures on Monday will be \nas much as 5 degrees below average for the mountains, inland \nvalleys, and high desert. High temperatures on Monday will range \nfrom the 70s near the coast to the 80s for the Inland Empire with \nthe lower deserts in the mid 90s. On Tuesday, high pressure over\nsouthern California will bring warming with decreasing mid and \nhigh clouds.\n\nAny surf impacts to the coast of Orange and San Diego Counties\nfrom Hurricane Polo would most likely be after the weekend. The\ncurrent track forecast through the weekend would most be outside\nof the the swell window the coast of Orange and San Diego \nCounties. There is greater spread in the track forecast beyond the\nweekend and any resulting potential swell and surf impacts along \nthe coast for early next week.",
